.TH OPENEIGRPD.CONF 5 "November 2026" "OpenEIGRP" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
openeigrpd.conf \- native OpenEIGRP named-mode configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/openeigrpd.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
A declarative OpenEIGRP configuration file containing named router instances,
IPv4/IPv6 unicast address families, interface configuration and base-topology
settings. Lines beginning with ! or # are comments. Nested scopes must be
closed with exit-af-interface, exit-af-topology, exit-address-family and exit.
Only the default Linux VRF is currently accepted.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
router eigrp example
 address-family ipv4 unicast autonomous-system 100
  eigrp router-id 192.0.2.1
  network 192.0.2.0 0.0.0.255
  af-interface eth0
   hello-interval 5
  exit-af-interface
 exit-address-family
exit
.fi
.SH VALIDATION
Run
.B openeigrpd-config -t -f /etc/openeigrpd.conf
to check the full file for syntax errors and unsupported directives before
attempting startup. A successful check does not establish that network
privileges, host providers or runtime semantic operations will succeed.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The native daemon and atomic SIGHUP configuration reload are not yet connected.
The standalone checker does not install routes or modify EIGRP runtime state.
See linux/specs/configuration.md for the supported directives and required
transaction semantics.
